Trihan said:
It's best to respond to replies on the assumption that nobody reading it knows the details of the plugins you're using. "Makai's Object Properties" won't mean anything to a lot of people.
Click to expand...
Hello, it is a plugin that allows me to use object properties instead of just the Global Variables that RPG Maker has to offer. To put it shortly, those are too few for me to use. So I use the plugin to allow those same Global Variables to host properties like objects do in JavaScript. Therefore, instead of assigning 1 single value to a Global Variable, I can assign thousands of such values, then call on them with ease.
Example:
maka.objVar.setProp(926,"_BnvlFmAfár_dmgTaken_Recorded",0);
maka.objVar.setProp(926,"_BnvlFmAfár_Ally_healing_Ratio",1.5);
maka.objVar.setProp(926,"_BnvlFmAfár_Chant_turnActive","GraceFromAfár");
This is a snippet from a small ability that allows me to add 3 values to 1 of those Variables, in this case, 926. I will be having dosens of thousands of such written in different text files (.txt extension). Only thing I need is to know a way of convincing RPG Maker MV to be able to read these bunches from those corresponding files as if they were written inside RPG Maker.

